Description: Compound target for Rockwell FactoryTalk / Allen-Bradley OT environments. Aggregates FactoryTalk Diagnostics, FT View SE + ME project files and runtime logs, and the rest of the FactoryTalk Services Platform stack (Activation, Linx, Historian SE, Batch, ViewPoint). Run this against any Windows HMI server or engineering workstation suspected of involvement in an OT incident.
Author: Raul B Netto (Cybolt DFIR)
Version: 1.0
Id: a221e8dd-4b3a-4fb5-a835-dbdf42e3706e
RecreateDirectories: true
Targets:
    -
        Name: FactoryTalk Diagnostics (common logging subsystem)
        Category: Logs
        Path: FactoryTalkDiagnostics.tkape
    -
        Name: FactoryTalk View SE and ME (HMI projects + runtime logs)
        Category: FileSystem
        Path: FactoryTalkViewSE_ME.tkape
    -
        Name: FactoryTalk Services (FTSP, Activation, Linx, Historian, Batch, ViewPoint)
        Category: Logs
        Path: FactoryTalkServices.tkape

# Documentation
# Usage:
#   kape.exe --tsource C: --target RockwellFactoryTalk ^
#            --tdest E:\EVIDENCE\<HOSTNAME> ^
#            --targetdir C:\KAPE\Targets ^
#            --zip E:\EVIDENCE\<HOSTNAME>\<HOSTNAME>-FTV ^
#            --hv nc,vm --vss
#
# Why a custom target exists:
#   There is no official RockwellFactoryTalk target in EricZimmerman/KapeFiles.
#   This compound target is the Cybolt DFIR answer for OT environments where
#   the affected host runs any FactoryTalk component. Pair with KapeTriage to
#   also collect standard Windows artifacts (event logs, registry, prefetch).
#
# Cross-references (CISA ICS Advisories):
#   ICSA-24-226-06 : FT View SE permission assignment (CVE-2024-7513)
#   ICSA-24-256-23 : FT View SE command injection RCE (CVE-2024-45824)
#   ICSA-25-028-03 : FT View ME command injection RCE (CVE-2025-24480)
#   SD1753 (10/2025): FT View ME + PanelView Plus 7 path traversal (CVE-2025-9063/9064)
#   SD1752 (10/2025): FT ViewPoint XXE (CVE-2025-9066)
